 in staging. The service was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service is healthy in all regions with an error rate of 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and work out why an unhealthy staging RC was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 44849, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0122ZFhfpEY1JzGr6ZKADsbv", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 44849, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0122ZFhfpEY1JzGr6ZKADsbv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 48316, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now live in all three regions, and the service is healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also lists two next steps: find the root cause in v2.3.1 before redeploying it, and work out why its release candidate reached production. That candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed health checks in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GdMCEbWuySo5YVd1Sphhf9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-a