"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now live in all three regions, and the service is healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also lists two next steps: find the root cause in v2.3.1 before redeploying it, and work out why its release candidate reached production. That candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed health checks in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}